2. CPU Utilization Problem
Answer
Problem

A system shows low CPU utilization (30%) even though processes are ready.

Scheduler log:

Ready → Waiting → Ready → Waiting → Ready ...
Debug Analysis
The processes repeatedly move between the Ready and Waiting states.
This indicates that the processes are I/O-bound, meaning they frequently request input/output operations.
While waiting for I/O to complete, the CPU remains idle, resulting in low CPU utilization.
Root Cause
I/O-bound Processes
        ↓
Frequent I/O Requests
        ↓
Processes Enter Waiting State
        ↓
CPU Remains Idle
        ↓
Low CPU Utilization (30%)
System-Level Optimization

1. Increase Multiprogramming

Load more CPU-bound processes into memory.
While one process waits for I/O, another process can use the CPU.

2. Use Asynchronous I/O

Allow processes to continue execution without blocking during I/O operations.

3. Improve CPU Scheduling

Use scheduling algorithms such as Multilevel Feedback Queue (MLFQ) or Round Robin with an appropriate time quantum to improve CPU usage.
Result
CPU Utilization Increased

CPU Idle Time Reduced

Improved System Throughput

Better Overall Performance
